From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] wificond: leave the radio alone at start

wificond restarts with zygote. After a framework restart the radio module was
still loaded, and CleanUpSystemState() (0001) waited for its unload, up to
15 s, before wificond registered its service. The new system_server tried to
start Wi-Fi meanwhile, found no wificond ("Failed to get reference to
wificond") and left Wi-Fi off until it was switched off and on by hand (Test
V39, 2026-10-15; the unload itself failed too, see system/core 0004).

At start wificond now only does AOSP's clean-up (supplicant stopped,
interfaces down). The framework tears the interfaces down itself when it
starts (tearDownInterfaces(), which unloads the module and waits for it) and
sets them up again if Wi-Fi is on. Asking for the unload here without waiting
instead would race the framework's load request.

--- a/server.cpp
+++ b/server.cpp
@@ -242,9 +242,11 @@
   supplicant_manager_->StopSupplicant();
   hostapd_manager_->StopHostapd();
   MarkDownAllInterfaces();
-#ifdef PW3_WIFI_MODULE_CONTROL
-  Pw3SetRadioEnabled(false);
-#endif
+  // PW3: the radio is not touched here. wificond restarts with zygote, and
+  // waiting for an unload at this point delayed the service's registration:
+  // the new framework found no wificond and left Wi-Fi off. The framework
+  // tears the interfaces down itself when it starts (tearDownInterfaces(),
+  // which unloads the radio module), and sets them up again if Wi-Fi is on.
 }
 
 bool Server::SetupInterface(InterfaceInfo* interface) {
